  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Deepak Shrivastava vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 22 January, 2024 Author: Anand Pathak Bench: Anand Pathak 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Before HON'BLE SHRI JUSTICE ANAND PATHAK ON THE 22 nd OF JANUARY, 2024 MISC. CRIMINAL CASE No. 56751 of 2023 BETWEEN:- DEEPAK SHRIVASTAVA S/O LATE SHRI GORISHANKAR SHRIVASTAVA, AGED ABOUT 40 YEARS, OCCUPATION: PRIVATE JOB TULSI COLONY BEHIND JAIL MORENA TEHSIL AND DISTRICT MORENA (MADHYA PRADESH) .....APPLICANT (BY SHRI RAJEEV SHRIVASTAVA - ADVOCATE ) AND THE STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH INCHARGE POLICE STATION THROUGH POLICE STATION S.T.F. BHOPAL (MADHYA PRADESH) .....RESPONDENTS (BY SHRI RAVINDRA SINGH KUSHWAH - DY.A.G. ) This application coming on for admission this day, the court passed the following: ORDER 1 .",
    "facts": "T he applicant has filed this third application under Section 439 of Code o f Criminal Procedure for grant of bail. Applicant has been arrested on 22.09.2023 by Police Station STF Bhopal, relating to Crime No.11/2019 for the offences punishable under Sections 420, 272, 273, 120-B of IPC and Section 51, 59 of Food Safety & Standard Act, 2006. Because of medical condition of his daughter on the fateful day he could not appear before the trial Court and arrest warrant has been issued against him.",
    "arguments": "2. It is the submission of learned counsel for applicant that it is a case of bail jump and applicant is suffering confinement since 22.09.2023 and suffered more than four months of incarceration. Earlier he suffered around one month as pretrial detention. Therefore, he already suffered sufficient period of incarceration."
  },
